IMPORT prelude

-- Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) -- pension age (s 23(5A)-(5D)), 10 years qualifying Australian residence (s 7(5)), qualification for
-- and payability of the age pension (ss 43, 44) with the assets and ordinary income tests of Pension Rate Calculator A (s 1064, Modules
-- A, E, G), the Commonwealth seniors health card (s 1061ZG, with the Seniors Health Card Income Test Calculator in s 1071), the
-- disability support pension (ss 94, 103(2)), jobseeker payment (s 593) and its liquid assets test waiting period (ss 14A, 598), youth
-- allowance age and the parental income test (ss 540, 543, 543A, 543B; s 1067G Modules A, F), and carer allowance for a disabled adult
-- (ss 954, 954A, 957A).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 232, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 17, 2025 (register id C2026C00336, in
-- 6 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04121.txt. The deposit's metadata warns that a version in force from
-- 20 September 2026 has no registered compilation yet, so amendments commencing on or after that date may be missing.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0005 in ../../../requirements.jsonl (priority 1): raised 9 times by the three Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave scenarios (chloe c079, c093; jake k086, k091, k092, k093, k095; daniel d020, d083), which ask: is he eligible for the
-- Age Pension, and for the seniors health card; what does JobSeeker require; what is the Disability Support Pension test and who decides
-- a borderline case; what does a carer get; which pension at 67; what is the parental income test. SCOPED to those questions and the
-- definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- Not encoded: the rest of a 6-volume Act. In particular: every payment rate and its indexation (ss 1190-1194), rent assistance, the
-- pension, energy and remote area supplements, the work bonus, deeming (ss 1076, 1077) and every rule for what counts as income or as an
-- asset (Parts 3.10, 3.12), the homeowner definition (s 11), disposal of assets, financial hardship (ss 1129, 1130), the income
-- maintenance period and ordinary waiting period for jobseeker payment, employment pathway plans and compliance (Administration Act),
-- independence for youth allowance (s 1067A), the maintenance income test (Module GA), carer allowance for children and its rate, the
-- Impairment Tables and the Adult Disability Assessment Tool (legislative instruments, not deposited), and review and appeal (Social
-- Security (Administration) Act 1999, not deposited).
-- INPUTS, because the Act does not state the operative figure: the maximum payment rates (Module B tables are base figures, indexed);
-- the assets value limits and income free areas actually in force (Tables G-1 and E-1 are base figures; s 1192(5C)-(5E) shows Table G-1
-- holds the figures "immediately before" 1 July 2017, indexed since); the seniors health card income limit actually in force (indexed
-- every 20 September); the parental income free area (fixed by the Family Assistance Act, cl 38N of Schedule 1); and -- THE DEPOSIT
-- HAS LOST THEM -- the reduction formulas of point 1064-E10 and Table G-2 column 3, the formula of point 1067G-F28 and the formula in
-- s 598(2A). Where a note or defined terms fix the shape of a lost formula, the shape is used and marked as an inference.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive encodings (the writing-l4-rules
-- skill was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public
-- use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Social Security Act 1991 -- the payments the Western Australian lives ask about`

§§ `Dates and ages`

-- Dates are written as numbers YYYYMMDD. A person "turns" an age on the anniversary of birth; age is counted in completed months.
-- (Birthdays on 29 February are not handled.)
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of` MEANS FLOOR (`d` DIVIDED BY 10000)

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month of` MEANS FLOOR (`d` DIVIDED BY 100) MINUS (`the year of` `d` TIMES 100)

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day of` MEANS `d` MINUS (FLOOR (`d` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES 100)

GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER, `today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`completed months of age` MEANS
        ((`the year of` `today` MINUS `the year of` `born`) TIMES 12)
    PLUS (`the month of` `today` MINUS `the month of` `born`)
    MINUS (IF `the day of` `today` LESS THAN `the day of` `born` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below nil` MEANS IF `a` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `a`

§§ `23(5A)-(5D) -- pension age`

-- (5A) Table--Pension age for men: born "On or before 30 June 1952" 65 years; "1 July 1952 to 31 December 1953" 65 years and 6 months;
-- "1 January 1954 to 30 June 1955" 66 years; "1 July 1955 to 31 December 1956" 66 years and 6 months; "On or after 1 January 1957" 67
-- years. (5B) A woman born before 1 July 1935: 60. (5C) women born 1 July 1935 to 31 December 1948: 60 years and 6 months rising by 6
-- months every 18 months to 64 years and 6 months. (5D) women born from 1 January 1949: the same five steps as men, from 65 years.
GIVEN `male` IS A BOOLEAN, `born` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`pension age in months` MEANS
    IF `born` AT MOST 19520630 AND (`male` OR `born` AT LEAST 19490101) THEN 780
    ELSE IF `born` AT LEAST 19570101 THEN 804
      ELSE IF `born` AT LEAST 19550701 AND `born` AT MOST 19561231 THEN 798
        ELSE IF `born` AT LEAST 19540101 AND `born` AT MOST 19550630 THEN 792
          ELSE IF `born` AT LEAST 19520701 AND `born` AT MOST 19531231 THEN 786
            ELSE IF `born` LESS THAN 19350701 THEN 720
              ELSE IF `born` AT MOST 19361231 THEN 726
                ELSE IF `born` AT MOST 19380630 THEN 732
                  ELSE IF `born` AT MOST 19391231 THEN 738
                    ELSE IF `born` AT MOST 19410630 THEN 744
                      ELSE IF `born` AT MOST 19421231 THEN 750
                        ELSE IF `born` AT MOST 19440630 THEN 756
                          ELSE IF `born` AT MOST 19451231 THEN 762
                            ELSE IF `born` AT MOST 19470630 THEN 768
                              ELSE 774

GIVEN `male` IS A BOOLEAN, `born` IS A NUMBER, `today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has reached pension age` IF
    `completed months of age` `born` `today` AT LEAST `pension age in months` `male` `born`

§§ `7(5) -- 10 years qualifying Australian residence`

-- s 7(5): "(a) the person has, at any time, been an Australian resident for a continuous period of not less than 10 years; or (b) the
-- person has been an Australian resident during more than one period and: (i) at least one of those periods is 5 years or more; and
-- (ii) the aggregate of those periods exceeds 10 years." Note the asymmetry: one period of exactly 10 years is enough; several periods
-- totalling exactly 10 years are not.
GIVEN `longest period in years` IS A NUMBER, `number of periods` IS A NUMBER, `aggregate in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has 10 years qualifying Australian residence` IF
        `longest period in years` AT LEAST 10
    OR  (    `number of periods` GREATER THAN 1
         AND `longest period in years` AT LEAST 5
         AND `aggregate in years` GREATER THAN 10)

§§ `43, 44 -- age pension: qualification and payability`

-- s 43(1): "A person is qualified for an age pension if the person has reached pension age and any of the following applies: (a) the
-- person has 10 years qualifying Australian residence; (b) the person has a qualifying residence exemption for an age pension; (c) the
-- person was receiving a widow B pension, a widow allowance, a mature age allowance or a partner allowance, immediately before reaching
-- that age". (Paragraph (d) and subsections (1A)-(4), for widows and former wife pensioners, are folded into (c)'s flag.)
DECLARE Senior HAS
    `is male` IS A BOOLEAN
    `born on` IS A NUMBER
    `has 10 years qualifying residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a qualifying residence exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was receiving a widow or partner payment before pension age` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the senior` IS A Senior, `today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is qualified for an age pension` IF
        `has reached pension age` (`the senior`'s `is male`) (`the senior`'s `born on`) `today`
    AND (    `the senior`'s `has 10 years qualifying residence`
         OR  `the senior`'s `has a qualifying residence exemption`
         OR  `the senior`'s `was receiving a widow or partner payment before pension age`)

-- Pension Rate Calculator A, Module A (1064-A1): maximum payment rate (Steps 1-4); "Apply the ordinary income test using MODULE E ...
-- the result is called the income reduced rate" (Steps 5, 8); "Apply the assets test using MODULE G ... the result is called the
-- assets reduced rate" (Steps 9, 10); Step 11: "the lower of the 2 rates, or the income reduced rate if the rates are equal, is the
-- provisional annual payment rate". Step 12's advance deductions and remote area allowance are not modelled.
-- 1064-A2, E2, G2: members of a couple are treated as pooling income and assets "on a 50/50 basis".
-- Module E: income excess = ordinary income less the free area (nil if not exceeding). The reduction formula of 1064-E10 is LOST in the
-- deposit ("A person's reduction for ordinary income is:" and nothing follows); it is taken here as an INPUT rate per dollar of excess.
-- Module G: assets excess = value of assets less the assets value limit (nil if not exceeding); 1064-G7 "disregard any part of the
-- excess that is not a multiple of $250". Table G-2 column 3 (the reduction) is LOST in the deposit; an INPUT rate per dollar of excess.
DECLARE Means HAS
    `maximum payment rate per year` IS A NUMBER
    `ordinary income per year` IS A NUMBER
    `ordinary income free area` IS A NUMBER
    `income reduction per dollar of excess` IS A NUMBER
    `value of assets` IS A NUMBER
    `assets value limit` IS A NUMBER
    `assets reduction per dollar of excess` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `own` IS A NUMBER, `partner's` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the couple's 50/50 share` MEANS (`own` PLUS `partner's`) DIVIDED BY 2

GIVEN `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assets excess` MEANS
    IF `m`'s `value of assets` AT MOST `m`'s `assets value limit` THEN 0
    ELSE FLOOR ((`m`'s `value of assets` MINUS `m`'s `assets value limit`) DIVIDED BY 250) TIMES 250

GIVEN `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income reduced rate` MEANS
    `not below nil` (`m`'s `maximum payment rate per year`
                     MINUS (`not below nil` (`m`'s `ordinary income per year` MINUS `m`'s `ordinary income free area`)
                            TIMES `m`'s `income reduction per dollar of excess`))

GIVEN `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assets reduced rate` MEANS
    `not below nil` (`m`'s `maximum payment rate per year` MINUS (`the assets excess` `m` TIMES `m`'s `assets reduction per dollar of excess`))

GIVEN `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the provisional annual payment rate` MEANS `the lower of` (`the income reduced rate` `m`) (`the assets reduced rate` `m`)

-- s 44(1): "an age pension is not payable to a person if the person's age pension rate would be nil" (subject to (2), the quarterly
-- supplement elections, not modelled).
GIVEN `the senior` IS A Senior, `today` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an age pension is payable` IF
        `is qualified for an age pension` `the senior` `today`
    AND `the provisional annual payment rate` `m` GREATER THAN 0

-- Table G-1, as printed: not member of a couple $250,000 (either homeowner) / $450,000 (neither homeowner); partnered $187,500 /
-- $287,500. These are base figures, indexed annually (Note 4; ss 1191-1194, 1203). They are NOT the limits in force on any scenario
-- date; the cases pass the limit in force as an input.
GIVEN `partnered` IS A BOOLEAN, `homeowner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Table G-1 base figure` MEANS
    IF `partnered`
    THEN (IF `homeowner` THEN 187500 ELSE 287500)
    ELSE (IF `homeowner` THEN 250000 ELSE 450000)

§§ `1061ZG, 1071 -- seniors health card`

-- s 1061ZG(1): qualified on a day if the person "(a) has reached pension age; and (b) is an Australian resident or a special category
-- visa holder residing in Australia; and (c) is in Australia; and (d) satisfies the seniors health card income test; and (e) is not
-- receiving a social security pension or benefit; and (f) is not receiving a service pension, income support supplement or a veteran
-- payment; and (g) is not subject to a newly arrived resident's waiting period". (2): not qualified if the person failed to give a copy
-- of an assessment when asked (s 1061ZJ), holds the Veterans' Entitlements Act card, or did not follow an accepted estimate with the
-- notice of assessment within 52 weeks.
-- s 1071, 1071-1: Step 1B = adjusted taxable income for the reference tax year plus any deemed income amount on long-term financial
-- assets; "Step 4. If the amount at step 1B is less than the person's seniors health card income limit, the person satisfies the
-- seniors health card income test. Step 5. If the amount at step 1B is equal to or exceeds the ... limit, the person does not". 1071-11:
-- for a member of a couple, "add the couple's adjusted taxable incomes ... and divide by 2". 1071-12 table: not member of couple
-- $90,000, partnered $72,000, plus $639.60 per dependent child; column 3 indexed every 20 September -- the limit in force is an INPUT.
-- The deemed income amount (1071-11A, 11B, via ss 1076, 1077) is an INPUT.
DECLARE CardClaimant HAS
    `is male` IS A BOOLEAN
    `born on` IS A NUMBER
    `is an Australian resident or protected SCV holder residing in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is partnered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `partner's adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `deemed income amount` IS A NUMBER
    `income limit in force` IS A NUMBER
    `is receiving a social security pension or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is receiving a service pension, income support supplement or veteran payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is subject to a newly arrived resident's waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is disqualified under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `c` IS A CardClaimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `satisfies the seniors health card income test` IF
    (    (IF `c`'s `is partnered`
          THEN `the couple's 50/50 share` (`c`'s `adjusted taxable income`) (`c`'s `partner's adjusted taxable income`)
          ELSE `c`'s `adjusted taxable income`)
     PLUS `c`'s `deemed income amount`)
    LESS THAN `c`'s `income limit in force`

GIVEN `c` IS A CardClaimant, `today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is qualified for a seniors health card` IF
        `has reached pension age` (`c`'s `is male`) (`c`'s `born on`) `today`
    AND `c`'s `is an Australian resident or protected SCV holder residing in Australia`
    AND `c`'s `is in Australia`
    AND `satisfies the seniors health card income test` `c`
    AND (NOT `c`'s `is receiving a social security pension or benefit`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `is receiving a service pension, income support supplement or veteran payment`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `is subject to a newly arrived resident's waiting period`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `is disqualified under subsection (2)`)

§§ `94, 103 -- disability support pension`

-- s 94(1): qualified if "(a) the person has a physical, intellectual or psychiatric impairment; and (b) the person's impairment is of 20
-- points or more under the Impairment Tables; and (c) ... (i) the person has a continuing inability to work; (ii) the Secretary is
-- satisfied that the person is participating in ... the supported wage system; and (d) the person has turned 16; and (da)" for a person
-- under 35 (or a reviewed 2008-2011 DSP starter) able to work 8 hours a week, whose youngest dependent child (if any) is 6 or over, "the
-- person meets any participation requirements that apply to the person under section 94A"; "(e)" a residence condition at first
-- satisfying (c); "(ea)" a current residence condition. (e) and (ea) are flags here.
-- (2): continuing inability to work if the Secretary is satisfied that "(aa) in a case where the person's impairment is not a severe
-- impairment ... the person has actively participated in a program of support"; "(a) in all cases -- the impairment is of itself
-- sufficient to prevent the person from doing any work independently of a program of support within the next 2 years; and (b) ... (i)
-- the impairment is of itself sufficient to prevent the person from undertaking a training activity during the next 2 years; or (ii)"
-- any training "is unlikely (because of the impairment) to enable the person to do any work independently of a program of support
-- within the next 2 years". (3A): when a CURRENT recipient is reassessed on a notice under s 63 of the Administration Act, and is not
-- a reviewed 2008-2011 DSP starter, "paragraph (2)(aa) of this section does not apply in relation to that assessment".
-- (3B): "severe impairment if the person's impairment is of 20 points or more under the Impairment Tables, of which 20 points or more
-- are under a single Impairment Table". (6): not qualified if the person brought about the inability with a view to obtaining the
-- pension or an exemption. The rating under the Impairment Tables (a legislative instrument, not deposited) is an INPUT.
DECLARE DSPClaimant HAS
    `age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `has a physical, intellectual or psychiatric impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `impairment points in total` IS A NUMBER
    `highest points under a single Impairment Table` IS A NUMBER
    `has actively participated in a program of support` IS A BOOLEAN
    `impairment prevents work independently of a program of support within 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `impairment prevents a training activity within 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `training is unlikely to enable work within 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `participates in the supported wage system` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is subject to participation requirements and fails them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the residence condition of paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the residence condition of paragraph (ea)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `brought about the inability to obtain the pension` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a reassessment of a recipient on a section 63 notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a reviewed 2008-2011 DSP starter` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `p` IS A DSPClaimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a severe impairment` IF
        `p`'s `impairment points in total` AT LEAST 20
    AND `p`'s `highest points under a single Impairment Table` AT LEAST 20

GIVEN `p` IS A DSPClaimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph (2)(aa) applies` IF
        (    (NOT `has a severe impairment` `p`)
         OR  `p`'s `is a reviewed 2008-2011 DSP starter`)
    AND (    (NOT `p`'s `is a reassessment of a recipient on a section 63 notice`)
         OR  `p`'s `is a reviewed 2008-2011 DSP starter`)

GIVEN `p` IS A DSPClaimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a continuing inability to work` IF
        ((NOT `paragraph (2)(aa) applies` `p`) OR `p`'s `has actively participated in a program of support`)
    AND `p`'s `impairment prevents work independently of a program of support within 2 years`
    AND (    `p`'s `impairment prevents a training activity within 2 years`
         OR  `p`'s `training is unlikely to enable work within 2 years`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `brought about the inability to obtain the pension`)

GIVEN `p` IS A DSPClaimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is qualified for disability support pension` IF
        `p`'s `has a physical, intellectual or psychiatric impairment`
    AND `p`'s `impairment points in total` AT LEAST 20
    AND (`has a continuing inability to work` `p` OR `p`'s `participates in the supported wage system`)
    AND `p`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 16
    AND (NOT `p`'s `is subject to participation requirements and fails them`)
    AND `p`'s `meets the residence condition of paragraph (e)`
    AND `p`'s `meets the residence condition of paragraph (ea)`

-- s 103(2): "If: (a) a person is receiving a disability support pension; and (b) another social security pension ... becomes payable to
-- the person; the disability support pension is not payable". Note 1: "Another payment type will generally not become payable to the
-- person until the person claims it." Nothing in ss 94-103 ends the DSP at pension age.
GIVEN `receiving disability support pension` IS A BOOLEAN, `age pension has become payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disability support pension remains payable` IF
        `receiving disability support pension`
    AND (NOT `age pension has become payable`)

§§ `593, 14A, 598 -- jobseeker payment and the liquid assets test waiting period`

-- s 593(1): qualified for a period if "(a) the person satisfies the Secretary that: (i) throughout the period the person is unemployed;
-- or (ii) subsection (1A) applies" (temporary incapacity with a job to return to); "(b) throughout the period the person satisfies
-- subsection (1AC)" -- the mutual obligation: "(i) the person satisfies the employment pathway plan requirements; (ii) the person
-- satisfies the Employment Secretary that the person is willing to actively seek and to accept and undertake paid work in Australia",
-- or is exempt from the plan requirements and would otherwise be willing; "(g) ... (i) is at least 22 years of age and has not reached
-- the pension age; and (ii) is an Australian resident or is exempt from the residence requirement"; "(i) the person was not in receipt
-- of a youth allowance during the period". Subject to ss 596-598.
DECLARE Jobseeker HAS
    `is male` IS A BOOLEAN
    `born on` IS A NUMBER
    `is unemployed or temporarily incapacitated under subsection (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies subsection (1AC)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an Australian resident or exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received youth allowance during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `liquid assets` IS A NUMBER
    `is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `served a waiting period that started in the preceding 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `comes from a continuous period of income support payments` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `j` IS A Jobseeker, `today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the qualification conditions for jobseeker payment` IF
        `j`'s `is unemployed or temporarily incapacitated under subsection (1A)`
    AND `j`'s `satisfies subsection (1AC)`
    AND `completed months of age` (`j`'s `born on`) `today` AT LEAST 264
    AND (NOT `has reached pension age` (`j`'s `is male`) (`j`'s `born on`) `today`)
    AND `j`'s `is an Australian resident or exempt`
    AND (NOT `j`'s `received youth allowance during the period`)

-- s 14A(1): liquid assets are "cash and readily realisable assets", including deposits and "(c) amounts due, and able to be paid, to the
-- person by, or on behalf of, a former employer of the person" (so unpaid redundancy pay counts); (2) a partner's liquid assets are
-- included. "maximum reserve ... (a) if the person is not a member of a couple and does not have a dependent child -- $5,000; or (b) in
-- any other case -- $10,000."
GIVEN `j` IS A Jobseeker
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum reserve` MEANS
    IF (NOT `j`'s `is a member of a couple`) AND (NOT `j`'s `has a dependent child`) THEN 5000 ELSE 10000

-- s 598(2A): "Work out the number of formula weeks (disregarding any fractions of a week) ... using the formula:" -- the FORMULA IS LOST
-- in the deposit; only its terms survive: "liquid assets", "maximum reserve amount", and "divisor ... (a) if the person is not a member
-- of a couple and does not have a dependent child -- $500; or (b) otherwise -- $1,000". INFERENCE: (liquid assets - maximum reserve
-- amount) / divisor, the only use of those three terms that gives weeks. (2B): "equal to or greater than 13 weeks ... is 13 weeks".
-- (1): the waiting period applies only if liquid assets EXCEED the maximum reserve. (4A): not if the person or partner was serving a
-- waiting period that started in the preceding 12 months. (6): not for a person who becomes qualified at the end of a continuous period
-- of income support payments. (5), severe financial hardship, is a discretion and is not modelled.
GIVEN `j` IS A Jobseeker
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the divisor` MEANS
    IF (NOT `j`'s `is a member of a couple`) AND (NOT `j`'s `has a dependent child`) THEN 500 ELSE 1000

GIVEN `j` IS A Jobseeker
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the liquid assets test waiting period in weeks` MEANS
    IF     `j`'s `liquid assets` AT MOST `the maximum reserve` `j`
        OR `j`'s `served a waiting period that started in the preceding 12 months`
        OR `j`'s `comes from a continuous period of income support payments`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the lower of` 13 (FLOOR ((`j`'s `liquid assets` MINUS `the maximum reserve` `j`) DIVIDED BY `the divisor` `j`))

§§ `540, 543, 543A, 543B -- youth allowance: study and age`

-- s 540(1): qualified for a period if throughout it the person "(i) is undertaking full-time study" (or is exempt, or satisfies (2), the
-- job-seeking limb), "(b) ... is of youth allowance age", "(d) ... is an Australian resident" or exempt. s 543: youth allowance age =
-- attained the minimum age and not the maximum age. s 543A(1): minimum age "(a) is at least 16 years old; or (b) is 15 years old and is
-- independent"; (2) under 18 also requires completed final year of school, "(b) is undertaking full-time study", an employment pathway
-- plan, or a new apprenticeship; (2AA) full-time SECONDARY study at 16 or 17 does not count unless independent, required to live away
-- from home, already receiving youth allowance, or not benefiting from family tax benefit (one flag here). s 543B(1)(c): maximum age for
-- a full-time student "is at least 25 years old"; (a), (d): 22 for others who are not new apprentices. (2), continuing past 25, and
-- (1)(b), (e) are not modelled.
DECLARE Student HAS
    `age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `is independent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is undertaking full-time study` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the study is a secondary course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an exception in subsection 543A(2AA) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has completed the final year of secondary school` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an Australian resident or exempt` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `s` IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has attained the minimum age for youth allowance` IF
        (`s`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 16 OR (`s`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 15 AND `s`'s `is independent`))
    AND (    `s`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 18
         OR  `s`'s `has completed the final year of secondary school`
         OR  (    `s`'s `is undertaking full-time study`
              AND ((NOT `s`'s `the study is a secondary course`) OR `s`'s `an exception in subsection 543A(2AA) applies`)))

GIVEN `s` IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has attained the maximum age for youth allowance` IF
    IF `s`'s `is undertaking full-time study` THEN `s`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 25 ELSE `s`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 22

GIVEN `s` IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is qualified for youth allowance as a full-time student` IF
        `s`'s `is undertaking full-time study`
    AND `has attained the minimum age for youth allowance` `s`
    AND (NOT `has attained the maximum age for youth allowance` `s`)
    AND `s`'s `is an Australian resident or exempt`

§§ `1067G -- youth allowance: the parental income test`

-- Module F, 1067G-F1: if the person is exempt (F3: a parent "is receiving a payment of pension, benefit, allowance or compensation
-- referred to in Module L", or ABSTUDY) or "the person's combined parental income does not exceed the person's parental income free
-- area", the result is nil; otherwise Submodule 6. F10: combined parental income sums each parent's taxable income, fringe benefits,
-- target foreign income, net investment loss, tax free pensions and reportable super contributions; F20 reduces it by maintenance paid.
-- F22: the parental income free area is the Family Assistance Act's cl 38N income free area -- an INPUT.
-- F27 (no parental income in common): the FORMULA IS LOST in the deposit; its Note survives: "Dividing by 130 is equivalent to dividing
-- by 26 (for 26 fortnights in a year) and dividing again by 5 (so that the parental income test result is only 20 cents for each dollar
-- of the excess)". INFERENCE from the Note: (combined parental income - free area) / 130, a fortnightly amount. F29: round "to the
-- nearest 10 cents (rounding a multiple of 5 cents upwards)".
-- F28 (parental income in common -- F26: a parent is also a parent of another person the test applies to; F31 deems an FTB child of a
-- parent to be one): the formula is LOST and no Note gives its shape; its result is an INPUT here.
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest 10 cents` MEANS FLOOR ((`x` TIMES 10) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 10

GIVEN `combined parental income` IS A NUMBER, `maintenance paid by a parent` IS A NUMBER, `parental income free area` IS A NUMBER,
      `a parent receives a Module L payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `has parental income in common` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the F28 result supplied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the parental income test result` MEANS
    IF     `a parent receives a Module L payment`
        OR (`combined parental income` MINUS `maintenance paid by a parent`) AT MOST `parental income free area`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `has parental income in common`
         THEN `the F28 result supplied`
         ELSE `rounded to the nearest 10 cents`
                  (((`combined parental income` MINUS `maintenance paid by a parent`) MINUS `parental income free area`) DIVIDED BY 130)

-- Module A, 1067G-A1 Step 13: take away "the greatest of" the reduction for parental income and the income reduction; "If that rate is
-- nil because of the taking away of a reduction described in paragraph (a) then youth allowance is not payable to the person." The
-- maximum payment rate (Modules B-D, indexed) and the person's own income reduction (Module H) are INPUTS; the maintenance income test
-- (Module GA, which can only add to the parental reduction up to the "MIT reducible amount") is not modelled.
GIVEN `maximum payment rate per fortnight` IS A NUMBER, `reduction for parental income` IS A NUMBER,
      `own income reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the provisional fortnightly youth allowance rate` MEANS
    `not below nil` (`maximum payment rate per fortnight`
                     MINUS (IF `reduction for parental income` AT LEAST `own income reduction`
                            THEN `reduction for parental income` ELSE `own income reduction`))

§§ `954, 954A, 957A -- carer allowance for a disabled adult`

-- s 954(1): qualified for carer allowance for a disabled adult (the care receiver) if "(a) the care receiver is an Australian resident;
-- (b) the care receiver is a family member of the person or is a person approved in writing by the Secretary"; "(c) the care receiver
-- has been assessed and rated under the Adult Disability Assessment Tool and given a score ... of at least 30, being a score calculated
-- on the basis of a professional questionnaire score of at least 12"; "(d) ... receives care and attention on a daily basis from the
-- person, or the person together with another person, in a private home that is the residence of the person and the care receiver";
-- "(f) the person is an Australian resident"; "(g) the person satisfies the carer allowance income test under section 957A".
-- s 23(14): for this Part a family member is a partner, parent, sister, brother or child (or a person the Secretary treats as one).
-- s 954A: where the home is NOT shared, the care must address special care needs of bodily functions or sustaining life, "on a daily
-- basis, for a total of at least 20 hours a week", the person's work must not be on wages at or above the relevant minimum wage, and
-- no one may be qualified for the care receiver under s 954.
-- s 957A Step 6: "The person satisfies the carer allowance income test if the amount at step 5 is less than $250,000" -- the sum of the
-- person's and (if a member of a couple) the partner's adjusted taxable income, plus any deemed income amount (an INPUT). Unlike the
-- seniors health card, the couple's incomes are ADDED, not halved, and the figure is stated, not said to be indexed.
DECLARE Carer HAS
    `care receiver is an Australian resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `care receiver is a family member or approved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ADAT score` IS A NUMBER
    `professional questionnaire score` IS A NUMBER
    `home is shared with the care receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gives care and attention daily` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours of care a week` IS A NUMBER
    `care addresses bodily functions or sustaining life` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is paid at or above the minimum wage for the care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `someone is qualified under section 954 for the care receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an Australian resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `partner's adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `deemed income amount` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `c` IS A Carer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `satisfies the carer allowance income test` IF
    `c`'s `adjusted taxable income` PLUS `c`'s `partner's adjusted taxable income` PLUS `c`'s `deemed income amount` LESS THAN 250000

GIVEN `c` IS A Carer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the common conditions are met` IF
        `c`'s `care receiver is an Australian resident`
    AND `c`'s `care receiver is a family member or approved`
    AND `c`'s `ADAT score` AT LEAST 30
    AND `c`'s `professional questionnaire score` AT LEAST 12
    AND `c`'s `is an Australian resident`
    AND `satisfies the carer allowance income test` `c`

GIVEN `c` IS A Carer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is qualified for carer allowance for a disabled adult` IF
        `the common conditions are met` `c`
    AND `c`'s `gives care and attention daily`
    AND (    `c`'s `home is shared with the care receiver`
         OR  (    `c`'s `hours of care a week` AT LEAST 20
              AND `c`'s `care addresses bodily functions or sustaining life`
              AND (NOT `c`'s `is paid at or above the minimum wage for the care`)
              AND (NOT `c`'s `someone is qualified under section 954 for the care receiver`)))
